> I was playing nethack in explore mode the other day, when I met a
> Mind Flayer that sucked my brains out.   Apart from killing me, I
> couldn't continue the game.   The questions I want to ask are, can I
> avoid this happening again (by wearing a helmet for example) and is
> this a bug?

Yes, that's what mind flayers are supposed to do.  Helmets will protect
you from them but only temporarily while giving you time to kill them.
I once got attacked by a mind flayer in explore mode.  I had a helmet
but it eventually sucked my brain out after repeated failures to kill
it and I had to abort the game.  Explore mode will restore your hit
points and thus let you continue after a normal death, but it won't
restore your stats (intelligence in this case).  Whether this is a
'bug' or not is up to the Dev Team.

p.s. Mind Flayers are my second most favorite monster on my genocide
	list after Master Liches.


